This is a test version, that tries to fix the "silent DMR" problem that happens sometimes; e.g when<br>a QSO talker remains silent (I'm not talking about kerchunkers).<br><br><br>You <strong class="text-strong">MUST</strong> report to this thread if this fixes or not that specific problem.<br><br><br><strong class="text-strong">This is based on the 2025/03/23 Beta version.</strong><br><br><br>The firmwares are available at: <strong class="text-strong">link removed because it does not fix the problem</strong><br>The voice prompts are available at: <a href="https://drive.proton.me/urls/CT7Y3QE8CC#ivbPuzbV8ty1" class="postlink">https://drive.proton.me/urls/CT7Y3QE8CC#ivbPuzbV8ty1</a><br><br><strong class="text-strong">NOTE</strong>: You <span style="text-decoration:underline">need</span> to use a CPS version greater or equal the the 2025/03/23. See the CPS section <a href="https://www.opengd77.com/viewforum.php?f=12" class="postlink">viewforum.php?f=12</a><br><br>For translators, the on-screen texts, voice prompts CSV are located at: <a href="https://drive.proton.me/urls/AFEPKF84F4#2ltiJXlnndiy" class="postlink">https://drive.proton.me/urls/AFEPKF84F4#2ltiJXlnndiy</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Sun Mar 23, 2025 4:59 pm</p><hr />
